From: Kerim Incedayi <k@kerim.me>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 12:16:57 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Fix T1 identifier parsing and document live preflight and
 ramdisk rejection

---
 docs/T1-EXPERIMENTAL.md | 44 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-----------
 scripts/t1-run.py       |  2 +-
 src/idevicerestore.c    |  6 +++++-
 src/t1.c                | 14 +++++++++----
 tests/test_t1.py        | 20 +++++++++++++++++++
 5 files changed, 69 insertions(+), 17 deletions(-)

diff --git a/docs/T1-EXPERIMENTAL.md b/docs/T1-EXPERIMENTAL.md
index 57ca1b2..7a674e9 100644
--- a/docs/T1-EXPERIMENTAL.md
+++ b/docs/T1-EXPERIMENTAL.md
@@ -1,7 +1,8 @@
 # Experimental T1 EmbeddedOS support (Linux only)
 
 This is a new implementation based on the public runbook, **not** the author's
-unpublished patch and **not yet validated on hardware**:
+unpublished patch. **Hardware preflight passed; provisioning is blocked at the
+restore ramdisk command**:
 https://gist.github.com/tigercosmos/ecbfe1fc20b7303c1808d3ab74af1f5b
 
 Scope is deliberately restricted to x619ap, chip 0x8002, board 0x12, Image4-capable
@@ -27,6 +28,10 @@ Implemented:
 - T1 signing uses the accompanying libtatsu verified-HTTPS API, restricted to
   https://gs.apple.com/TSS/controller?action=2 with certificate/hostname checking,
   no redirects or HTTP fallback, bounded timeouts, and failure on transport errors.
+  The tool includes Apple's public Root CA for this connection only. The CA was
+  downloaded over normally verified HTTPS from Apple's PKI link and its DER
+  SHA-256 checked: b0b1730ecbc7ff4505142c49f1295e6eda6bcaed7e2c68c5be91b5a11001f024.
+  No system-wide certificate trust change or disabled verification is required.
 
 - Identity/build restriction and explicit ECID selection; validate the physical
   recovery device and restored HardwareInfo against the selected chip/board/ECID.
@@ -72,15 +77,16 @@ privately as unhandled-message.plist. No acknowledgement is sent for rejected
 stores. This is not proof that every valid T1 FDR message is supported.
 
 The iBEC → restore-ramdisk flow reuses upstream component personalization, with a
-fresh TSS request after re-enumeration. Its timing and signing behavior have not
-been observed on this T1. The strict supported-message list may reject additional
+fresh TSS request after re-enumeration. iBEC upload, recovery re-enumeration and
+subsequent signing succeeded on this T1. The restore ramdisk command was rejected
+with `Ramdisk image not valid`; the restored session was never reached. The strict supported-message list may reject additional
 legitimate messages; review the private evidence before adding support.
 
 The installed libimobiledevice 1.4.0 provides reverse-proxy APIs and protocol
 versions 2/1 are attempted. No extra reverse-proxy patch was invented: the report
 mentions patched support without publishing its details. FDR connectivity and
-Apple service acceptance are still unverified. No actual FDR data or signing
-request was generated during development.
+Apple FDR service acceptance are still unverified. Apple signing and local image
+construction passed on hardware, but no FDR data has been generated.
 
 The generic restore helpers used for NOR/FUD still have upstream behavior and
 parsers. These patches do not claim a security audit of the whole toolchain.
@@ -182,10 +188,14 @@ with this T1's ECID; debug, custom signing servers, erase, keep-personalized, ig
 errors and other generic restore flags are rejected. The executable creates no
 host disk targets and accepts no block-device restore destination.
 
-Before pass A/B, a reviewed private usbmuxd instance must own the mux socket with
+Before pass A/B, a reviewed private usbmuxd instance must own the selected mux socket with
 `USBMUXD_T1_RECOVERY=1`; the system instance must not compete. The patch changes
 only the opt-in libusb device-class filter; product-ID and mux-interface checks
-remain. This broader discovery applies to Apple's matching product IDs, so detach
+remain. The tested setup used an isolated root-private UNIX socket, passed as
+`-S /private/path/mux.sock` to usbmuxd and
+`USBMUXD_SOCKET_ADDRESS=UNIX:/private/path/mux.sock` to the launcher. Its config,
+PID handling and logs were isolated too; no system daemon was installed or
+replaced. The daemon was stopped after the attempt. This broader discovery applies to Apple's matching product IDs, so detach
 unrelated Apple devices during a future experiment.
 
 Between successful passes and before replay, wait at least ten seconds. Any
@@ -199,11 +209,22 @@ with failed internal storage remains unverified even in the original report.
 ## Development result
 
 Patched libirecovery, libtatsu, usbmuxd and idevicerestore compiled locally.
-All 22 idevicerestore offline tests and the libtatsu mock-transport test passed.
+All 24 idevicerestore offline tests and the libtatsu mock-transport test passed.
 Earlier gcc static analysis with strict warnings passed for the initial T1 C
 modules. The compiled inspection mode accepted the checksum-verified Apple
-package's x619ap 14Y901 resources. No live signing, provisioning, FDR, memboot or
-Touch Bar test has been performed with these patches.
+package's x619ap 14Y901 resources. The live preflight passed after correcting the
+ECID argument format and supplying Apple's official CA to the signing connection.
+One provision attempt loaded iBEC and obtained a fresh ticket, then stopped at
+`ramdisk`; its private console reported `Ramdisk image not valid`. The original
+restore ramdisk SHA-384 and its digest in the Apple ticket match the manifest.
+The precise reason for device rejection remains unresolved; no further uploads
+were attempted. No restored session, NORData request, FDR generation or phase-14
+memboot occurred. The saved pair remains incomplete and cannot be replayed.
+
+The test sent `setenv auto-boot false` and `saveenv` to the T1 before the ramdisk
+failure. This is T1 state, distinct from the unchanged Linux boot configuration.
+No previous value was captured, so automatic reversal would be a guess. The T1
+remains in 05ac:1281 recovery. No personalized image was installed on EFI.
 
 The separate USB was formatted for a private live file backup of home, /etc and
 /boot, with partition metadata, the Linux encryption header and package list.
@@ -216,7 +237,8 @@ The local ACPI table defines the T1 reset method at
 `\_SB.PCI0.XHC1.RHUB.ASOC.FRST`: it toggles EC.SOCR with 15 ms and 600 ms waits,
 and has no explicit Return. The accompanying acpi_call patch handles a successful
 method with no output object instead of dereferencing NULL. It compiled against
-the running kernel; the module has not been loaded and FRST has not been called.
+the running kernel; the module was loaded and unloaded successfully without
+calling FRST. No reset was performed.
 Verification of this table is specific to this machine, not permission to call
 the same method on arbitrary models. T1 already enumerates in recovery here, so
 no reset is needed for preflight.
diff --git a/scripts/t1-run.py b/scripts/t1-run.py
index d6dc31a..645bf46 100644
--- a/scripts/t1-run.py
+++ b/scripts/t1-run.py
@@ -55,7 +55,7 @@ def main():
         env['IDEVICERESTORE_T1_PRIVATE'] = str(args.private)
         if args.fdr_input:
             env['IDEVICERESTORE_T1_FDR_INPUT_DIR'] = str(args.fdr_input)
-        command += ['-i', format(select_ecid(), 'x')]
+        command += ['-i', hex(select_ecid())]
     command.append(str(args.firmware.resolve()))
     # ECID stays out of console output. Root/process monitors can still see argv.
     try:
diff --git a/src/idevicerestore.c b/src/idevicerestore.c
index c68c3b6..dcfbdd5 100644
--- a/src/idevicerestore.c
+++ b/src/idevicerestore.c
@@ -1909,7 +1909,11 @@ int main(int argc, char* argv[])
 					client->ecid = 0;
 				}
 				if (client->ecid == 0) {
-					logger(LL_ERROR, "Could not parse ECID from '%s'\n", optarg);
+					if (t1_requested()) {
+                    logger(LL_ERROR, "Could not parse T1 ECID\n");
+                } else {
+                    logger(LL_ERROR, "Could not parse ECID from '%s'\n", optarg);
+                }
 					return EXIT_FAILURE;
 				}
 			}
diff --git a/src/t1.c b/src/t1.c
index 66e5985..1171ae3 100644
--- a/src/t1.c
+++ b/src/t1.c
@@ -59,8 +59,11 @@ static int strict_command(irecv_client_t r, const char *cmd, int breq)
     if (global_quit_flag) return -1;
     size_t size = strlen(cmd) + 1;
     if (size > 256) return -1;
-    return irecv_usb_control_transfer(r, 0x40, breq, 0, 0,
-        (unsigned char *)cmd, size, 10000) == (int)size ? 0 : -1;
+    int transferred = irecv_usb_control_transfer(r, 0x40, breq, 0, 0,
+        (unsigned char *)cmd, size, 10000);
+    if (transferred != (int)size)
+        fprintf(stderr, "T1 command %s: transferred=%d expected=%zu\n", cmd, transferred, size);
+    return transferred == (int)size ? 0 : -1;
 }
 
 static int send_component_command(struct idevicerestore_client_t *c,
@@ -151,9 +154,9 @@ static plist_t capture_pair(struct idevicerestore_client_t *c, plist_t identity)
 
 int t1_preflight(struct idevicerestore_client_t *c, plist_t identity, int fd)
 {
-    if (fresh_tss(c, identity)) return -1;
+    if (fresh_tss(c, identity)) { status("preflight signing failed; no firmware uploaded"); return -1; }
     plist_t pair = capture_pair(c, identity);
-    if (!pair) return -1;
+    if (!pair) { status("preflight image validation failed; no firmware uploaded"); return -1; }
     int rc = save_plist(fd, "preflight-only.plist", pair);
     plist_free(pair);
     if (!rc) status("preflight passed: Apple ticket and local image validated; no firmware uploaded");
@@ -369,6 +372,8 @@ int t1_start(struct idevicerestore_client_t *c)
     }
     close(logfd);
     mode_t previous_umask = umask(077);
+    /* Signing diagnostics stay behind the private stdout/stderr redirection. */
+    tss_set_debug_level(1);
     int rc = -1; plist_t pair = NULL, input = NULL;
     status("experimental mode; logs are private");
     if (input_path) {
@@ -426,6 +431,7 @@ int t1_start(struct idevicerestore_client_t *c)
     fflush(NULL);
     dup2(status_fd, STDOUT_FILENO); dup2(saved_err, STDERR_FILENO);
     close(status_fd); status_fd = -1; close(saved_err); close(fd);
+    tss_set_debug_level(0);
     umask(previous_umask);
     return rc;
 }
diff --git a/tests/test_t1.py b/tests/test_t1.py
index 6594cc5..001673e 100644
